  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: baa6e19cfc6944f42a3cb999ff4499bd, type: 3}
  m_Name: KidneysInfo
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::OrganInfoData
  organName: Kidneys
  overview: The kidneys are two bean-shaped organs, each about the size of a fist,
    responsible for filtering waste and excess fluid from the blood.
  structure: "\u2022\tRenal cortex and medulla\r\n\u2022\tNephrons\r\n\u2022\tRenal
    pelvis and ureter"
  organFunction: "\u2022\tFilters waste from blood\r\n\u2022\tRegulates fluid and
    electrolyte balance"
  didYouKnow: Your kidneys filter around 200 quarts of fluid every 24 hours, which
    produces about 1 to 2 quarts of urine.
